  "_": "Hit areas under 44px that the phone touch baseline tolerates today, per platform (Issue #1712). test/phone-touch-baseline-browser.test.mjs walks every phone-cell state in test/lib/states.mjs on WebKit at 390x844 and measures each control kind's reach across and down, the smallest over the kind's instances. A key is '<state> | <kind>' and its value is [across, down] in px. A kind with no entry is held to 44px; a recorded kind fails once it drops more than 2px under its entry, or under 43px on an axis that already met 44px. Only short targets are recorded, so the file only shrinks: when a fix lands, drop the entries the test reports as gone or met. A platform with no section fails and prints the entries it measured for each state, which seeds that section.",
